$report=@('# Art continuation, 2026-10-11','','This is a new worker-2 art candidate continuation. It preserves the previous R1 report, GLBs, browser captures, Blender renders, and failed attempts. It is not visual acceptance, provenance approval, or parent admission.','','## Candidate changes','','The continuation updates floor material, wall/desk/plant palette, hex panel geometry and emission, desk/shelf bevels, drawer fronts, floor monstera leaf silhouettes, and shelf ivy density. The carpet texture was generated by `source/environment/generate-carpet-texture.py` and embedded by the Blender export.','','## Exports and checks','','Blender 5.2.2 LTS completed `evidence/build-attempt-06/` with exit code 0. The process log is `evidence/environment-execution-attempt-06.log`. The resumed inspector receipt is `evidence/export-inspection-resumed-20261011-attempt-01.json`; glTF Validator 2.0.0-dev.3.10 reports zero errors and zero warnings for each of six GLBs. Authored-versus-exported transforms pass 129 checks for group A, 84 for group B, 33 for on-demand projects, 246 each for full and mobile room outputs, and 67 for the unchanged fixture export. These checks establish export structure and transforms only.','','The fixture receipt `evidence/fixture-attempt-03/blender-checks.json` reports zero desk-interior hits and grounded soles in all eight authored clips; `turn_to_visitor` and `greeting_nod` hand clearances are 0.16 m and 0.3312 m. Its eight 60 Hz clips total 1,040 samples. Exact fit and chair-seat intersections remain in the source JSON; these are not visual or behavior acceptance.','','The full-room candidate keeps `group_a_root` and `desk` at origin, `desk_top` at (0, 0.725, -1.15) m, `chair-root` at (0.3, 0, -0.36) m, door hinge at (-1.65, 0, 1.8) m with `door_leaf` parented below it, and `painting-pivot` at (2.08, 1.75, -0.4) m. The unchanged fixture export remains candidate-only. Authored interaction pivots are present in the world GLB; the separate accepted interaction animation assets were not edited.','','Five changed world exports were copied byte-for-byte to full SHA-256-named paths and are referenced by both `app/public/asset-manifest.json` and this revision `manifest.json`. The fixture candidate remained byte-identical at its existing versioned path. Current manifest and file comparisons are in `evidence/publication-verification-attempt-06.json`. All five changed assets remain `approved: false`, `status: candidate`.','','## Visual evidence and limitation','','Existing browser captures are in `evidence/browser-art-attempt-02/`, including before/after home renders at 1440×1000 and 390×844 and the other four home viewports. That report used older asset-manifest SHA-256 `2f846c6ddf5c0a1cb1f85b31c4dbf27a4400d8aca4f0f6009374d3f38e401027` and older asset URLs. Those images are not evidence for attempt 06. Parent review of them noted pale washed-out hex panels, a sparse/blocky room, and excess ceiling/floor in 390×844 framing.','','No revised browser capture was run. Parent asked that capture wait until the runtime-owned framing interface settles. Camera and lighting source is owned by the runtime lane, so this report does not claim visual success. Six refreshed viewport images are NOT RUN; independent visual/provenance review and parent admission remain pending.','','## Current candidate URLs','','See `app/public/asset-manifest.json`; its SHA-256 is recorded in `evidence/publication-verification-attempt-06.json`. Candidate URLs are hash-versioned. No historical public GLB was overwritten.') -join [Environment]::NewLine
[System.IO.File]::WriteAllText($reportPath,$report,[System.Text.UTF8Encoding]::new($false))
